    "body": "Stopped at Step 7 because an upstream gate failure repeated.\n\nThe quick gate failed `docs_troubleshooting::troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources`.\nThe targeted `cargo xtask gate test` run failed the same test again.\nThe unchanged test reads `site/content/guide/troubleshooting.md`.\nUpstream moved that file to `site/content/guide/reference/troubleshooting.md` in commit `89b43e04d`.\n\nThe broad gate also failed `operations::threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit` before posting.\nIts APocket3D fixture requests 20 mm stock depth with tool BN-0600, whose shank starts at 15 mm.\nBoth failing test files match upstream/main `6f8b309dc`.\nNo unrelated files were changed.\n\nThe local RichAuto patch passes 13 post pins and all 8 conformance tests.\nThe initial pins failed before implementation.\nThe absent-post and upstream-registry mutations each failed, then passed after restoration.\nAll 23 targeted mutations also failed, then passed after restoration.\nClippy passed for camcraft-app and camcraft-post with warnings denied.\nThe patch adds 13 NC goldens and changes no existing NC or CL files.\n\nThe uncommitted patch remains on branch `issue/1914-richauto` in `.claude/worktrees/issue-1914` in the CamcraftCodex checkout.\nIt adds a metric, G54, single-tool post with expanded drilling and named refusals.\nNo hardware was exercised.\nNo commit, push, or PR was made.\nSteps 8 and 9 remain undone.\nClaim released; the issue remains open.\n",
