    "body": "Stopped at Step 7 after an unrelated gate failure repeated.\n\nThe quick gate failed docs_troubleshooting::troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources.\nThe exact targeted repeat failed the same test again.\nThe page quotes the missing source stem \"was imported incomplete - closed shell\".\nThe test and page match branch base 31f8d03d without changes.\nThe shared upstream/main ref advanced to c86d6db3 during testing.\nNewer upstream commit 92430ff0 changes this troubleshooting heading.\nI did not merge it because Step 7 requires stopping after a repeated unrelated failure.\n\nThe local RichAuto patch passes 38 post tests and all 8 conformance tests.\nThe initial 17 pins failed before implementation because the post was absent.\nThe G89 expansion and modal-feed pins also failed before their fixes.\nAll 29 mutation scenarios failed with the old behavior and passed after restoration.\nClippy passed for camcraft-app and camcraft-post with all targets and warnings denied.\nThe patch adds 19 inspected NC goldens and 5 refusal goldens.\nIt changes no existing NC or CL files.\nNo hardware was exercised.\n\nThe uncommitted patch remains on branch issue/1914-richauto-a11 in /home/mikekinney/CamcraftPool/.claude/worktrees/issue-1914.\nIt adds the metric, G54, single-tool RichAuto A11 post, expanded drilling including G89 feed retract, spindle dwell, and named refusals.\nNo commit, push, or PR was made.\nSteps 8 and 9 remain undone.\nClaim released; the issue remains open.\n",
